{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender font drawing blender font drawing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md","fileName":"Blender Font Drawing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Font Drawing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Viewport Drawing API]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender font drawing blender font drawing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md","fileName":"Blender Font Drawing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Font Drawing","heading":"Blender Font Drawing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Font drawing turns application data into readable viewport annotations. A reusable helper accepts two-dimensional coordinates, text, size, and a font identifier, then configures and draws the string through Blender's font API.\n\nWorld-space data must first be projected into the viewport's two-dimensional region. After conversion, labels can follow an object's origin or a measurement midpoint as the view changes. Checking that projection returned a visible point prevents the drawing function from failing when the target lies outside the current view.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Viewport Drawing API","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Font Drawing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__no